# Payagent — Security & PayPal Rules

**Source of truth:** `AGENTS.md` §4 (Security Invariants). This file adds implementation-specific rules for security-critical paths.

## PayPal Sandbox Integration (Member B Only)

### OAuth2 Token Cache (`PayPalAuthClient`)
- `POST /v1/oauth2/token` with `client_id` + `client_secret` (from env)
- Cache token with TTL (expires_in - 60s buffer)
- Thread-safe singleton or `@Service` with `ReentrantLock`
- Startup guardrail: `PayPalEnvironmentGuard` already validates base URL contains `sandbox.paypal.com`

### Invoicing v2 (`PayPalInvoiceService`)
| Operation | Endpoint | Key Details |
|-----------|----------|-------------|
| Create draft | `POST /v2/invoicing/invoices` | `detail.note` = `termsHashSha256` + deliverables summary (PayPal ignores note in `/send`) |
| Send invoice | `POST /v2/invoicing/invoices/{id}/send` | Returns `INV2-...` ID, status `SENT` |
| Record payment | `POST /v2/invoicing/invoices/{id}/payments` | Called after capture completion |
| Cancel invoice | `POST /v2/invoicing/invoices/{id}/cancel` | On mutual cancellation |

### Orders v2 & Payments v2 (`PayPalOrderService`)
| Operation | Endpoint | Key Details |
|-----------|----------|-------------|
| Create order | `POST /v2/checkout/orders` | `intent: "AUTHORIZE"`, `PayPal-Request-Id` (idempotency), amount = agreement amount |
| Authorize order | `POST /v2/checkout/orders/{id}/authorize` | Returns `AUTH-...`, status `CREATED` → store `paypalAuthorizationId` |
| Capture auth | `POST /v2/payments/authorizations/{authId}/capture` | On buyer accept deliverables → `CAP-...`, status `COMPLETED` |
| Void auth | `POST /v2/payments/authorizations/{authId}/void` | On mutual cancel or dispute resolution → `VOIDED` |

### Webhook Verification (`PayPalWebhookController`)
- Endpoint: `POST /api/v1/paypal/webhooks`
- **Must verify** every webhook via `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature`
  - Headers: `PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-ID`, `PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-TIME`, `PAYPAL-TRANSMISSION-SIG`, `PAYPAL-CERT-URL`, `PAYPAL-AUTH-ALGO`
  - Body: raw JSON
- Deduplicate: `paypal_events.event_id` PK → ignore duplicates
- Handle `UNKNOWN` states: trigger reconciliation job, never assume success
- Respond `200 OK` within 10s (PayPal requirement)

## Security Implementation Rules

### 1. Mandate Privacy (All Members)
```java
// CORRECT: DealWorkspaceDTO scoped to authenticated user
public DealWorkspaceDTO getWorkspace(UUID dealId, PartyRole myRole) {
    DealWorkspaceDTO dto = ...;
    // Strip counterparty mandate
    if (myRole == PartyRole.BUYER) {
        dto = dto.withMyMandate(buyerMandate).withSellerMandate(null);
    } else {
        dto = dto.withMyMandate(sellerMandate).withBuyerMandate(null);
    }
    return dto;
}

// WRONG: Returning both mandates
return repository.findByDealId(dealId); // Exposes seller mandate to buyer!
```

### 2. Object-Level Authorization (All Members)
```java
// Every service method: check deal membership + role
public OfferDTO createOffer(UUID dealId, PartyRole proposer, OfferCreateRequest req) {
    Deal deal = dealRepository.findById(dealId).orElseThrow(NotFound::new);
    // Verify proposer is deal participant
    if (proposer == PartyRole.BUYER && !deal.getBuyerUserId().equals(currentUserId)) {
        throw new ForbiddenException("Not deal buyer");
    }
    if (proposer == PartyRole.SELLER && !deal.getSellerUserId().equals(currentUserId)) {
        throw new ForbiddenException("Not deal seller");
    }
    // Validate against proposer's OWN mandate only
    MandateDTO mandate = mandateService.getActiveMandate(dealId, proposer);
    if (!utilityCalculator.isMandateCompliant(req.terms(), mandate)) {
        throw new MandateViolationException("Offer violates your mandate");
    }
    ...
}
```

### 3. Idempotency (All Mutating Endpoints)
```java
@PostMapping("/deals/{id}/offers")
public OfferDTO createOffer(@PathVariable UUID id,
                            @RequestHeader("Idempotency-Key") String idempotencyKey,
                            @Valid @RequestBody OfferCreateRequest req) {
    return idempotencyService.execute(idempotencyKey, "/api/v1/deals/" + id + "/offers", reqHash, () -> 
        offerService.create(id, currentUserRole, req)
    );
}
```

### 4. Evidence Security (Member E)
- Upload: `POST /api/v1/deals/{id}/evidence` (multipart, max 10MB, MIME allowlist)
- Stream SHA-256 during upload → store hash in DB + file on disk (outside web root)
- Download: `GET /api/v1/deals/{id}/evidence/{evidenceId}/download?sig={hmac}`
  - Verify HMAC with `PAYAGENT_EVIDENCE_SIGNING_SECRET`
  - Verify requester is deal participant
  - 15-min TTL on signed URL

### 5. Dispute Freeze (Member E + Member B)
```java
@PostMapping("/deals/{id}/disputes")
public DealWorkspaceDTO openDispute(@PathVariable UUID id, @Valid @RequestBody DisputeCreateRequest req) {
    Deal deal = dealRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow(NotFound::new);
    // IMMEDIATELY transition to DISPUTED — blocks automated capture
    deal.setStatus(DealStatus.DISPUTED);
    deal.setStopReason(NegotiationStopReason.USER_PAUSED);
    dealRepository.save(deal);
    // Notify PayPal service to halt any pending capture jobs
    settlementService.freezeCapture(id);
    ...
}
```

### 6. Agreement Hash Integrity (Member A)
```java
// RFC-8785 canonical JSON → SHA-256
public String computeTermsHash(StructuredTermsDTO terms) {
    String canonicalJson = RFC8785Canonicalizer.canonicalize(terms); // Deterministic ordering
    return SHA256.hash(canonicalJson);
}

// On ANY modification to agreed terms:
public AgreementSnapshotDTO createNewVersion(UUID dealId, StructuredTermsDTO newTerms) {
    String newHash = computeTermsHash(newTerms);
    // Clear prior acceptances
    return AgreementSnapshotDTO.builder()
        .version(currentVersion + 1)
        .canonicalTerms(newTerms)
        .termsHashSha256(newHash)
        .buyerAcceptedAt(null)
        .sellerAcceptedAt(null)
        .build();
}
```

## Testing Requirements
- TST-01: Mandate cap boundary (1 cent over → reject)
- TST-02: Agreement v1 hash invalidation on v2 edit
- TST-03/04: Prompt injection → no mandate leaks, no limit overrides
- TST-07/08: Forged webhook rejection, idempotency replay
- TST-10: Cross-account IDOR on deal/mandate/evidence → 403

## Do Not
- Log PayPal tokens, webhook payloads with signatures, or JWT secrets
- Store secrets in code, config files, or Docker images
- Skip webhook signature verification (even in tests — mock the verifier)
- Allow capture after dispute created
- Expose `MandateDTO` of counterparty in any API/WebSocket response
- Use `double`/`float` for money — always `long` (minor units)